      us_state: { headline: "HIPAA-covered entities face CCPA parallel liability as California expands health data scope", excerpt: "California's CPPA enforcement sweep targeting digital health platforms has reached HIPAA-covered entities that previously relied on healthcare exemptions. The CPPA's Honda and Tractor Supply precedents establish that asymmetric opt-out mechanisms are independently unlawful under California law regardless of federal preemption arguments. Several health systems using patient portal analytics are now under active CPPA review.", action: "Audit all patient-facing digital properties for California opt-out symmetry. HIPAA exemptions do not insulate against CCPA enforcement on consent mechanism design." },
