      cross_border: { headline: "EU-US health data transfers require updated DPAs following EDPB pseudo-adequacy review", excerpt: "The EDPB's interim review of the EU-US Data Privacy Framework found that health data transfers require supplementary contractual safeguards beyond the DPF's baseline protections. Healthcare organizations transferring patient data to US cloud processors must update Data Processing Agreements to include health-specific provisions covering Article 9 lawful basis, sub-processor restrictions, and deletion schedules. The compliance deadline is July 1, 2026.", action: "Update all DPAs with US healthcare processors to include Article 9 supplementary provisions. Standard DPF reliance alone is insufficient for health data after the EDPB interim review." },
