      litigation: { headline: "EU health data subjects pursue GDPR Article 82 compensation claims against clinical AI providers", excerpt: "German courts have issued the first enforceable Article 82 GDPR compensation awards against clinical AI providers for non-material damage caused by automated diagnosis recommendations. A Munich Regional Court decision awarded €8,500 per claimant where AI-assisted triage delayed treatment. The decision creates a litigation pathway that plaintiffs' counsel across five EU member states are now actively pursuing.", action: "Review clinical AI deployment documentation for Article 22 GDPR compliance. Where automated processing substantially affects clinical decisions, ensure human review is documented and auditable." },
