      gdpr: { headline: "IAB TCF under coordinated DPA enforcement as Belgian, French, and Spanish regulators act simultaneously", excerpt: "The Belgian DPA's second-phase TCF ruling, French CNIL enforcement against programmatic platforms, and the Spanish AEPD's consent string audit program constitute a coordinated European challenge to the IAB's Transparency & Consent Framework. EU adtech operations relying on TCF 2.2 for Article 6 lawful basis face an unstable legal foundation. The EDPB's pending TCF opinion may invalidate TCF consent strings retroactively.", action: "Commission an urgent legal basis review for all EU programmatic inventory. Do not wait for the EDPB's TCF opinion — begin transitioning to alternative consent infrastructure for EU audiences now." },
      ai_act: { headline: "EU AI Act's Article 5 prohibition on manipulative AI captures behavioral targeting recommendation systems", excerpt: "The EU AI Office's February 2026 guidance on Article 5 prohibited AI practices specifically identifies behavioral targeting systems that exploit psychological vulnerabilities or unconscious biases as falling within the prohibition on manipulative AI. The guidance targets recommendation algorithms that optimize for engagement at the expense of user autonomy. Three major DSPs received formal AI Office inquiries in Q1 2026.", action: "Conduct an AI Act Article 5 risk assessment on all behavioral targeting and recommendation optimization algorithms deployed to EU audiences. Systems that optimize on engagement signals may fall within the prohibited manipulation category." },
      childrens: { headline: "FTC children's adtech enforcement escalates with age-adjacent audience targeting guidance", excerpt: "The FTC's February 2026 COPPA policy statement on age verification introduces new obligations for advertising platforms that reach audiences with a substantial proportion of under-13 users, even where the platform is not 'directed to children.' The FTC's Google/YouTube $30M settlement established the template. Platforms with youth-skewing audience demographics face enforcement regardless of formal age-gate status.", action: "Assess all audience segments for age composition. The FTC's COPPA enforcement now targets platforms with youth-skewing demographics regardless of formal age-gate status. Implement children's content exclusion lists for all programmatic campaigns." },
